title: $:/mf/gen/CLI command/mf metarecord get
catalog: CLI command
target: mf metarecord get
summary: Read: -i <uuid> → full JSON; -q/none → UUIDs (--select for fields)

!! Reference

```
Read: -i <uuid> → full JSON; -q/none → UUIDs (--select for fields)

Usage: mf metarecord get [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --select <SELECT>
          Print full metadata restricted to these fields, or '*' for all

      --sort <SORT>
          Sort key field[:asc|desc]; repeatable (query selectors only)

      --limit <LIMIT>
          Stop after N metarecords; when more match, print `next-cursor <token>` on stderr

      --cursor <CURSOR>
          Resume after a previous read's `next-cursor` token, to read a scope by batches with --limit. Valid only for the same query and --sort. Query selectors only (-q, or none)

      --count
          Print how many metarecords the selector matches, instead of them. One round-trip, exact, and O(1) on the index — the count a walk needs per question. Query selectors only (-q, or none)

      --values
          Print the selected field's raw values, one per line

      --tsv
          Print one tab-separated row per metarecord (first value of each --select field). Requires --select with a field list — except with --resolve-tree, where it prints `uuid<TAB>path` instead of bare paths. The requirement is checked in the command (clap cannot make it conditional), so it is still a usage error

      --resolve-tree <RESOLVE_TREE>
          Resolve this tree_ref field of each selected metarecord to its root-relative path(s), one per line (the bulk form of `mf path`). Needs a selector (-q or -i)

  -h, --help
          Print help
```
